From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] users: Local Accounts with one's own account first, Add in
 the header bar

Plinius: the Users panel (a row on Accounts, next to Online Accounts) is
called Local Accounts and is a list: Your Account with a row named
after one's username, Other Accounts below, each opening its page. One's
own page keeps the account part only (the ways to unlock are on Lock &
Unlock) and is called by the username.

"Add" in the header bar opens Add User as a page. The account comes from
plinius-add-user (plinius-account) through pkexec instead of
AccountsService's CreateUser: useradd would hand out the user IDs 1000
and up, which are Android's on the phone. The helper takes 32012 and up,
adds the groups of the phone's devices and sets the password in the same
step, so there is a single password prompt. The password is always set
in the dialog (no "User sets password on first login"): the screen lock
needs it, and plinius-greeter cannot set one at the first login.
